# Devoted Druid under Solemnity: "Counters can't be put on artifacts, creatures, enchantments, or lands" (CR 122.6, 101.2), so
# the Druid's "Put a -1/-1 counter on this creature" can't be paid (CR 118.3) and its untap ability can't be activated (the
# ruling). Bot1 casts the Druid on turn 1 off Forest and Mox Emerald and Solemnity on turn 3, then taps the Druid for {G}:
# its untap, offered in the scenario without Solemnity, is refused.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Devoted Druid
Plains
Solemnity
Forest x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Devoted Druid.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Solemnity.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Devoted Druid.Activate(Ability: {T})
? Bot1.Mana = {G}
! Bot1.Battlefield.Devoted Druid.Activate(Ability: -1/-1)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Devoted Druid.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Devoted Druid.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Mana = {G}
